<!--Post: 747--><!--Time: 1092494047-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST747"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 7:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jan. 19, 1991: Delores &#34;Dee&#34; Davis, 62, was abducted from her home a half-mile east of Park City. She was found 13 days later under a bridge in northern Sedgwick County. She was strangled, and her feet, hands and knees were bound with pantyhose. The killer cut her outside telephone lines, then threw a brick through a glass door at the rear of her home. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 747-->
<!--Post: 776--><!--Time: 1092670369-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST776"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 16, 2004 - 8:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Possible BTK victim.  A difference in each crime might keep you from getting caught.  Though the BTK rarely takes the victim outside the home he may have done it for this one. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 776-->
<!--Post: 788--><!--Time: 1092725711-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST788"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 16, 2004 - 11:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Taking outside would be a large difference, yes.  <BR> <BR>Abduction even a larger one. Hold on. How do they know she was &#34;abducted?&#34;  <BR> <BR>Read closely, it sounds like she may have been killed in her home and then dumped. I would think under cloak of darkness. Abductions happen quickly, usually at gunpoint. Why cut the phone lines? <BR> <BR>Nothing like detailed reporting! This one does sound less than BTK than others, yes. I can&#39;t quite rule it out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 788-->
<!--Post: 1119--><!--Time: 1097210010-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1119"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 07, 2004 - 9:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ms. Davis is reported to have worked just a few doors down from Nancy Fox&#39;s place of employment, the Law Co.  All of Kansas seems to be one big coincidence in relation to its homicides.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1119-->
<!--Post: 1238--><!--Time: 1097861862-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1238"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxtrotnem<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxtrotnem<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 15, 2004 - 10:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i remember this crime and followed it closely. it is really scary to me because it has alot of similarities with the MARINE HEDGE crime. both women lived in pk city, both women single lived alone and in their 50s. both women killed in the home and dumped out in the country. both women bound similarly. both women&#39;s phone lines were cut and both women last ate at a resteraunt called red coach inn. but the kicker is sedgwick county sheriff dept refuses to see any connection and both murders are unsolved. Ms Hedge&#39;s car was found in wichita and Ms Davis&#39; car was returned to her driveway with keys on the hood and completely spotless of prints or fibers. now i&#39;m no investigator but DUH!!!! does anyone else see similarities here?????????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1238-->
<!--Post: 1240--><!--Time: 1097881459-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1240"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 15, 2004 - 4:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve included a link for both women, they both have been compared with BTk similarities.  Hope these links are useful.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/news/local/crime_courts/8411738.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/news/local/crime_c ourts/8411738.htm</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/news/local/crime_courts/8411738.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/eagle/news/local/crime_c ourts/8411738.htm</a> <BR> <BR>wichitan <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1240-->
<!--Post: 1241--><!--Time: 1097881838-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1241"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 15, 2004 - 4:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->First sorry for the X2 links, but on that link there is this: <BR> <BR>Oct. 25, 1980: Barbara A. Smith, 37, was found beaten to death in her home at 1151 S. Waverly. There was no sign of forced entry. The killer set two small fires in the kitchen that burned themselves out. <BR> <BR>2 small fires huh, sounds kind of like the carole molde case.  The two small fires anyway. <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
